{"term":"dress","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:541c47e24229693725","definition":"To put clothes (or, formerly, armour) on (oneself or someone, a doll, a mannequin, etc.); to clothe.","example":"He was dressed in the latest fashions.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["attire","don","accouter","address","apparel","array","attire","beclothe","clothe","dight","don","garment","dress","enrobe","equip","invest","put on","robe","slip on","vest"],"antonyms":["strip","undress","denude","despoil","dismantle","disrobe","divest","doff","peel","put off","strip","strip down","strip off","unclothe","undress"],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively, reflexive","register":"also, figuratively, reflexive, transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:04592c1b20ee0c233f","definition":"To design, make, provide, or select clothes (for someone).","example":"The fashion designer was proud to have dressed the queen for the charity event.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:106a303524e338bced","definition":"To arrange or style (someone's hair).","example":"[Domitian] after his manner, with a cheerfull countenance and grieved heart, received the newes: being inwardly pricked, to think that his later counterfet triumph of Germany, wherin certain ſlaves bought for mony were attired and their haire dreſſed as captives of that country, was had in deriſion and iuſtly skorned abroad: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:62ee4fc05ecb78da26","definition":"To adorn or ornament (something).","example":"It was time to dress the windows for Christmas again.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be40c41f0b14f02d2a","definition":"To apply a dressing to or otherwise treat (a wound); (obsolete) to give (a wounded person) medical aid.","example":"[T]he Mayd / His readie vvound with better ſalues new dreſt, / Daily ſhe dreſſed him, and did the beſt / His grieuous hurt to guariſh, that ſhe might, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bandage","put a bandage on"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:497c129da84758072c","definition":"To fit or prepare (something) for use; to render (something) suitable for an intended purpose; to get ready.","example":"Now when the towne his ſommonds did diſdain, / To conquer it perforce he plyde his pain: / And their, th’Inginers haue the Trepan dreſt, / And reared vp the Ramme for batterie beſt: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9761384c03d358274d","definition":"To cultivate or tend to (a garden, land, plants, etc.); especially, to add fertilizer or manure to (soil); to fertilize, to manure.","example":"Gard[ener]. Oh what pitie is it that he had not ſo trimde, / And dreſt his land as vve this garden at time of yeare / Do vvound the barke, the skinne of our fruit trees, […] Queene. Oh I am preſt to death through vvant of ſpeaking / Thou old Adams likeneſſe ſet to dreſſe this garden, / How dares thy harſh rude tong ſound this vnpleaſing nevvs?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ade6e524f6ba605bb5","definition":"To cut up (an animal or its flesh) for food.","example":"\"I'll be with you,\" said Coo, \"never fear me.\" Jack went home and dressed a noble fish dinner, and got out plenty of his best foreign spirits, enough for that matter to make twenty men drunk.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:37764962d6c53985da","definition":"To prepare (food) for cooking or eating, especially by seasoning it; specifically, to add a dressing or sauce (to food, especially a salad).","example":"Old vvom[an]: [O]nce vppon a time his daughter was ſtollen avvay, and hee ſent ſo long, that he ſent all his men out of his Land. / Frol[icke]: VVho dreſt his dinner then?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f489c9c27fb365e75","definition":"To design, make, or prepare costumes (for a play or other performance); also, to present (a production) in a particular costume style.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:03de5c651021b38a4c","definition":"To prepare (a set) by installing the props, scenery, etc.","example":"Mallory, all night long, single-handedly painted and dressed the set so that at eight o'clock Sunday morning when we arrived to make breakfast in the kitchen, there she was sound asleep on the davenport in the set, every prop in place.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"sou