underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa69c8f44792b44736","definition":"To break in and train (a horse or other animal) for use.","example":"Oh how it ernd my hart when I beheld, / In London ſtreetes, that Coronation day, / VVhen Bullingbroke rode on Roane Barbarie. / That horſe, that thou ſo often haſt beſtride. / That horſe, that I ſo carefully haue dreſt.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1e06709a100af83475","definition":"To prepare (oneself); to make ready.","example":"[S]yr Gawayns ſpere brak ⸝ but ſir marhaus ſpere helde ⸝ And therwith ſyre Gawayne and his hors ruſſhed doune to the erthe ⸝ And lyghtly ſyre Gawayne roſe on his feet ⸝ and pulled out his ſwerd ⸝ and dreſſyd hym toward syr Marhaus on foote ⸝ […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, reflexive","register":"intransitive, obsolete, reflexive","wordFamily":["bride dress","dressable","dress down","dressed","dresser","dressing","dressing down","dressing-down","dress off","dress out","dress the part","dress up","field dress","hairdresser","outdress","overdress","redress","undress","undresser","undressing","xdress","hairdress","underdress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl